Article 2 (Duties of the Committee) The Constitutional Court Information System Deliberation Committee (hereinafter referred to as the "Committee") shall deliberate on the following matters: <Amended on April 27, 2015; March 22, 2021>
1. Basic plans for informatization of the affairs of the Constitutional Court;
2. Determination of important policies concerning informatization of the affairs of the Constitutional Court;
3. Annual informatization implementation plans and plans for execution of informatization budgets;
4. Matters concerning the operation and improvement of the website;
5. Matters concerning improvement of relevant statutes and systems;
6. Matters concerning information security, including information and communications networks and personal information;
7. Other matters deemed necessary by the Chairperson for informatization.
